<!--
  Chinese (Traditional) strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The reference country is Taiwan (plan, section 6.1), so the words are those of Taiwan, also for Hong Kong and Macao.
  The text uses "您" where a pronoun is necessary, full-width punctuation, the quotation marks 「」, and a space between
  Chinese characters and Latin letters or digits, as Chinese iOS does. Chinese has only the CLDR plural form "other".
-->
